{"title":"2024 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(Detailed_Explanation)_🚀⚡📊\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_by_MathTalks_Now\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video by MathTalks_Now</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(easy_to_digest)_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution  (easy to digest) by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Parshwa\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution  by Parshwa</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution  by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four squares of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a833bf1f7c89d83444455f7f6b560e2d9faf91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 7, 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are arranged in increasing size order so that their left edges and bottom edges align. The squares alternate in color white-gray-white-gray, respectively, as shown in the figure. What is the area of the visible gray region in square units?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e0c32b9dd52758b61dd87c199e00db7b42fbd1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(150); filldraw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--cycle,gray(0.7),linewidth(1)); filldraw((0,0)--(9,0)--(9,9)--(0,9)--cycle,white,linewidth(1)); filldraw((0,0)--(7,0)--(7,7)--(0,7)--cycle,gray(0.7),linewidth(1)); filldraw((0,0)--(4,0)--(4,4)--(0,4)--cycle,white,linewidth(1)); draw((11,0)--(11,4),linewidth(1)); draw((11,6)--(11,10),linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,(11,5),fontsize(14pt)); draw((10.75,0)--(11.25,0),linewidth(1)); draw((10.75,10)--(11.25,10),linewidth(1)); draw((0,11)--(3,11),linewidth(1)); draw((5,11)--(9,11),linewidth(1)); draw((0,11.25)--(0,10.75),linewidth(1)); draw((9,11.25)--(9,10.75),linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(4,11),fontsize(14pt)); draw((-1,0)--(-1,1),linewidth(1)); draw((-1,3)--(-1,7),linewidth(1)); draw((-1.25,0)--(-0.75,0),linewidth(1)); draw((-1.25,7)--(-0.75,7),linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(-1,2),fontsize(14pt)); draw((0,-1)--(1,-1),linewidth(1)); draw((3,-1)--(4,-1),linewidth(1)); draw((0,-1.25)--(0,-.75),linewidth(1)); draw((4,-1.25)--(4,-.75),linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(2,-1),fontsize(14pt)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e047879287b9e78cb51e3d82f6b7130ac065b1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 42 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 45\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 49\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 50\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We work inwards. The area of the outer shaded square is the area of the whole square minus the area of the second largest square. The area of the inner shaded region is the area of the third largest square minus the area of the smallest square. The sum of these areas is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/95633fa0d1a0b80eefa9abbed7e848048d4cad4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 4^2 = 100 - 81 + 49 - 16 = 19 + 33 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 52}\\]\" width=\"483\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>This problem appears multiple times in various math competitions including the AMC and MATHCOUNTS.\n</p><p>-Benedict (countmath1) ~Nivaar and anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In solution 1, we can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference_of_squares\" title=\"Difference of squares\">Difference of squares</a> to get the answer, rather than calculating the squares of the numbers:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c117a580ec1de88e68f622644efe532f6236dbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 4^2 = (10 - 9)(10 + 9) + (7 - 4)(7 + 4) = 1\\cdot19 + 3\\cdot11 = 19 + 33 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 52}\\]\" width=\"623\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~anabel.disher\n</p><p>minor edits by Sowthistle2011&#160;:)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solve for the areas for each square inside the larger one , and then subtract the areas of the white regions from the areas of each square:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/f/f0f77a5413873f171a139517f2351ffe0aad7887.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(10^2 + 7^2) - (9^2 + 4^2) = 149 - 97 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 52}\\]\" width=\"347\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>-MrTechguyPCMT and anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can calculate it as the sum of the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> smaller trapezoids and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> larger trapezoids. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/700260a89bb96e26af11b7f5bfb448d4fa1499c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\left(\\cfrac{(7+4)(7-4)}{2}\\right)+2\\left(\\cfrac{(10+9)(10-9)}{2}\\right)=10^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 4^2 = 19 + 33 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 52}\\]\" width=\"634\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>-SahanWijetunga\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/bSPWqeNO11M?si=HIzlxPjMfvGM5lxR\">https://youtu.be/bSPWqeNO11M?si=HIzlxPjMfvGM5lxR</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3MtJRXIIxyM\">https://youtu.be/3MtJRXIIxyM</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28Detailed_Explanation.29_.F0.9F.9A.80.E2.9A.A1.F0.9F.93.8A\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(Detailed_Explanation)_🚀⚡📊\">Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Youtube Link ⬇️\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZNAm6x17gro\">https://youtu.be/ZNAm6x17gro</a>\n</p><p>~ ChillGuyDoesMath&#160;:)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_.28Goes_through_full_thought_process.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/q64dg8YAJbE\">https://youtu.be/q64dg8YAJbE</a>\n</p><p>~mr_mathman\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_by_MathTalks_Now\">Video by MathTalks_Now</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video by MathTalks_Now\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=crn37TRMLv4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=crn37TRMLv4</a>\n</p><p>-rc1219\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BaE00H2SHQM?si=F37qz7vyfRgZm-1u&amp;t=469\">https://youtu.be/BaE00H2SHQM?si=F37qz7vyfRgZm-1u&amp;t=469</a>\n</p>\n<pre>~Math-X\n</pre>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5ZIFnqymdDQ?si=vSpf507